cl. 1. Ā. (Dhātup. ii, 6) ना॑थते, TS.; Kāṭh. &c. (˚ति, MBh.; Kathās.; pf. ननाथ; aor. अनाथीत्; fut. नाथिष्यति, or नाथिता Gr.; inf. नाथितुम्, Kathās.; ind.p. -नाथ्य, Prab.)
to seek aid, approach with prayers or requests (loc.), TS.; Kāṭh.;
to ask, solicit, beg for (gen. of thing, MBh. iii, 126, 30; cf. Pāṇ. ii, 3, 55; dat. of th˚, Vop.; with 2 acc. Naiṣ. iii, 25);
 to have power, be master, Dhātup. :
Caus. नाथयति, to cause a person to ask for anything i.e. to grant a request (acc.), BhP. (B.), ii, 9, 25.
